summary.value:
This work proposes Visual Instrumental Variable Learning for confounding-resistant domain generalization, which introduces instrumental variables to address the challenge of identifying confounders. The optimization process is decoupled into three stages:
(i) The first stage utilizes frequency-based augmentation to learn causal factors under the constraints of MMD and classification loss;
(ii) The second stage aims to learn implicit visual instrumental variables using three designed loss functions;
(iii) The third stage trains a regressor to learn causal factors responsible for classification.
Experiments are conducted on PACS, VLCS, Office-Home, and Digits-DG.

